[MUSIC]

2
00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.530
You should now have a
better understanding of

3
00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.590
the basic components of
stock option contracts,

4
00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.360
as well as the common
language used by

5
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.015
buyers and sellers
of these products.

6
00:00:30.015 --> 00:00:32.115
But now you may be asking,

7
00:00:32.115 --> 00:00:35.815
what do I have to gain or lose
by trading in this market?

8
00:00:35.815 --> 00:00:38.645
Well, before buying
or selling an option,

9
00:00:38.645 --> 00:00:40.760
you should note that as a rule,

10
00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.355
investors are required
among other actions,

11
00:00:43.355 --> 00:00:45.740
to read a copy of
the characteristics

12
00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:48.260
and risks of
standardized options,

13
00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:53.575
also known as the Options
Disclosure Document or ODD.

14
00:00:53.575 --> 00:00:56.780
This booklet which relates
solely to options issued by

15
00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:00.200
the Options Clearing
Corporation or OCC,

16
00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.480
provides insights into
the options market,

17
00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.555
including the risks faced
by both buyers and sellers,

18
00:01:05.555 --> 00:01:07.340
margin requirements,

19
00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:10.710
tax considerations,
and other topics.

20
00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:14.240
Among other functions and
services the OCC serves as

21
00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.040
a central counterparty and

22
00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:17.990
all listed options transactions.

23
00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:21.170
Meaning it provides a guarantee
that a trade will settle,

24
00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:22.760
should an option writer fail to

25
00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:25.070
satisfy their part
of the contract.

26
00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:27.380
You can find out more
about the OCC from

27
00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:28.790
their website as well as

28
00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:31.865
obtain the options
disclosure document.

29
00:01:31.865 --> 00:01:35.030
In general, the
advantages and risks of

30
00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:36.860
trading options mainly depend

31
00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:38.680
on your reason for using them.

32
00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:41.330
Are you looking more
generating additional income,

33
00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:43.910
for example, or hedging
an existing position?

34
00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:45.440
Are you bullish or bearish on

35
00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:46.820
the market and want to speculate

36
00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:50.125
on a stock price over a
fixed period of time?

37
00:01:50.125 --> 00:01:51.920
Well we'll dig more deeply into

38
00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:53.675
these subjects later
in the course.

39
00:01:53.675 --> 00:01:55.265
It's important to note that

40
00:01:55.265 --> 00:01:57.380
what you stand to gain or lose in

41
00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:58.940
the options market is

42
00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:01.490
largely tied to your
market strategy,

43
00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:02.870
as well as at what price

44
00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:04.520
the underlying security needs

45
00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:06.500
to be for you to break-even.

46
00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:10.085
That is neither gain nor
lose on your investment.

47
00:02:10.085 --> 00:02:11.930
Some of the main motives for

48
00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:14.840
options traders to enter the
market include the potential

49
00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:17.825
for enjoying games that
are relatively lower cost

50
00:02:17.825 --> 00:02:19.070
and buying the underlying

51
00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:21.545
security outright in
the stock market,

52
00:02:21.545 --> 00:02:23.975
as well as generating
additional income

53
00:02:23.975 --> 00:02:27.034
and protection against
existing exposure.

54
00:02:27.034 --> 00:02:31.025
Taking a closer look at the
four basic options contracts,

55
00:02:31.025 --> 00:02:32.915
we can see that as a buyer,

56
00:02:32.915 --> 00:02:35.030
your maximum gain is equivalent

57
00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:37.310
to the seller's maximum loss.

58
00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:39.650
In other words, while
the risk faced by

59
00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:41.415
a contract holder is limited

60
00:02:41.415 --> 00:02:43.525
to the premium paid
to the seller,

61
00:02:43.525 --> 00:02:46.670
the writer's risk
can be substantial.

62
00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:49.070
Recall that as an option seller,

63
00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:51.695
you may receive a
relatively small premium

64
00:02:51.695 --> 00:02:52.790
and exchange for acting

65
00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:54.515
as either buyer or seller

66
00:02:54.515 --> 00:02:56.915
to the holder of the
option contract.

67
00:02:56.915 --> 00:02:59.750
If the contract owner
approves correct and

68
00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:02.420
is locked in at a better
price to buy or sell,

69
00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:03.860
it may cost you more as

70
00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:06.500
an option seller in the
open market to fulfill

71
00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.990
your obligation to sell
the required shares

72
00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:12.110
for that delivery unless
you already hold them.

73
00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:15.455
If you're an unhedged
seller of a call option,

74
00:03:15.455 --> 00:03:19.100
you could feasibly
face unlimited losses.

75
00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:21.350
For that reason, options trading

76
00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:23.875
is not suitable
for all investors.

77
00:03:23.875 --> 00:03:26.480
There are naturally
several other advantages

78
00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:28.580
for traders to engage
in the options market,

79
00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:31.910
as well as numerous additional
risks that you may face.

80
00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:33.980
Given this, we urge
you to conduct

81
00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.240
your own due diligence

82
00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:37.175
depending on your
financial conditions,

83
00:03:37.175 --> 00:03:40.815
investment objectives,
or other requirements.

84
00:03:40.815 --> 00:03:42.530
As you progress
through the course,

85
00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:44.810
you'll also gain a
further understanding of

86
00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:47.630
the nuances that
underlie the upsides and

87
00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:50.180
pitfalls of options
trading for a host of

88
00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:53.630
popular trading strategies
and combinations.

